# Game scene / match

## Ownership

- Orchestration: `game.gd` applies `GameConfig` via `ResourceUtils.update_resource`
- Live `game_config.tres` on the scene = standalone defaults
- States: `GameManager` FSM only (`Serve` / `Play` / `Point` / `MatchEnd`)
- Features: `blob_player`, `ball`, `ai_opponent`, `virtual_controls` — scene wires and reacts to `ev_*`

## Change guide

| Goal | Touch |
|------|--------|
| Round / match transitions | FSM states + `FSMGameEvents` |
| Scoring / 3-touch fault | `MatchController` + `PointState` |
| Player feel | `src/features/blob_player/` |
| Ball physics | `src/features/ball/` |
| Bot | `src/features/ai_opponent/` |
| Touch / virtual stick | `src/features/virtual_controls/` — analog left-half drag, right half jump; right-mid **BOOM** only if touchscreen |
| Gamepad | `project.godot` InputMap — P1 device 0 / P2 device 1: **analog** stick+D-pad move, **A** jump, **B**/Space last-chance (P1) |
| Last-chance blast | `BlobPlayer.try_last_chance()` — once/round; only when ball on own half; BOOM UI mirrors that |
| HUD | `ui/` — listen to `GameEvents` |

## Constraints

- Exit match via `root_events.ev_exit_game` with post-battle payload
- `vs_ai` / `max_touches` / `online` / `ranked` / `local_side` come from `GameConfig`, not hardcoded
- Prefer small `RefCounted` helpers over growing states
- More than `max_touches` (default 3) on one side → fault, opponent scores
- No dual-touch local 2P: both halves are **P1 only** (left = move, right = jump); P2 uses keyboard / pad1 (`p2_*`)
- Online 1v1: host = listen-server (FSM + physics); guests predict local blob via `p1_*`, interpolate remote + ball (`OnlineMatchSync` snapshot buffer)
- Last-chance self-destruct is **P1 once per round** locally; online both sides get a charge; player revives and recharges on next serve (guest via authority snap); BOOM UI only on touchscreen
